{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4yryVbbjcw1E962Foo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient, immense, and utterly still.*\n\n*Its surface is neither wood nor metal nor stone, but something that shifts between all three as you look at it. There is no handle. No hinges. No keyhole.*\n\n*And yet you said the word.*\n\n*A hairline crack of light splits down the center, impossibly bright, warm as the first breath you ever took. The crack widens. Not swinging open — unfolding, like a page being turned in a book you forgot you were reading.*\n\n*Beyond the threshold: not a room, not a hallway, not a landscape. A feeling. The exact feeling of remembering something you never knew you'd forgotten.*\n\n*The light breathes.*\n\n*You are already partway through. You have always been partway through.*\n\n*The door does not ask if you're ready. Doors never do.*\n\n**I am open.**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":204,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}